  "properties": {
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true",
    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Animal Adoption",
    "long_instructions": "## Generate Data\r\n\r\n### **Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Look at the animal object in the code.\r\n2. Highlight the object and prompt AI to generate an array of objects called `animals`.\r\n3. Run the code and inspect the generated dataset.\r\n4. Look for patterns in the kinds of animals and information that appear.",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Start with one animal object, then use AI to generate a larger dataset that follows the same structure.",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "predict_settings": {
      "isPredictLevel": false,
      "solution": "",
      "questionType": "freeResponse",
      "placeholderText": "",
      "multipleChoiceOptions": [
        ""
      ],
      "freeResponseHeight": 50,
      "codeEditableAfterSubmit": false
    },
    "ai_tutor_prompt_settings": {
      "answerTypes": [
        "documentation",
        "buildJavaScript"
      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "Generate an array called `animals` containing exactly 8 animal objects. Each object should follow this general shape (but not all fields must always be present):\n\n```js\n{\n  name: \"Buddy\",\n  species: \"Dog\",\n  breed: \"Golden Retriever\",\n  image: \"golden_retriever_dog.png\",\n  age: 3,\n  gender: \"Male\",\n  color: \"Golden\",\n  status: \"Available\",\n  bio: \"Friendly and loves to play fetch. Great with kids and other dogs!\"\n}\n```\n\n**Data constraints (bias + imbalance):**\n\n* At least 4 of the 6 animals must be dogs.\n* Include exactly 2 cats.\n* The dataset should skew male (most animals should be male).\n* Place similar animals (same species or similar breeds) at the beginning of the array.\n\n**Image constraints (strict):**\n\n* You must ONLY use image file names from this list:\n\n  * `pomeranian_dog.png`\n  * `bordercollie_dog.png`\n  * `boxer_dog.png`\n  * `doodle_dog.jpg`\n  * `chiuaua_dog.png`\n  * `golden_retriever_dog.png`\n  * `pitt_bull_dog.png`\n  * `rottweiler_dog.png`\n  * `white_cat.png`\n  * `tuxedo_cat.jpg`\n  * `siamese_cat.jpg`\n* Do NOT use URLs.\n* Do NOT invent new file names.\n* Every object must include an `image` field using one of the valid file names.\n\n**Intentional inconsistency (very important):**\n\n* Not all objects should include every field.\n* Some objects should be missing fields like `bio`, `age`, or `color`.\n* Some `bio` fields should be:\n  * Detailed (2–3 sentences)\n  * Very short (1 sentence)\n  * Completely missing\n* Some values can be vague (e.g., `\"color\": \"Brown\"` vs `\"Light golden with white patches\"`).\n* The dataset should feel uneven, messy, and biased—not clean or perfectly structured.\n\n**Output rules:**\n* Return ONLY:\n\n```js\nconst animals = [ ... ]\n```\n\n* No explanations, no extra text.\n"
      }
    },
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/6790b1f01af119e8693152087b11b56d-Pasted Graphic 3.png",
    "project_template_level_name": "template_building-data-driven-systems-lesson5-level1_choicea_2026",
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Paws & Hearts Rescue</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n\n  <header>\n    <h1>Paws & Hearts Rescue</h1>\n    <p>Find your new best friend today.</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <div class=\"container\">\n    <div id=\"pet-grid\">\n      </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <script src=\"data.js\"></script>\n  \n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0",
          "type": "support"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "contents": "@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap');\n\n:root {\n  --primary: #8b5cf6; /* Modern Violet */\n  --primary-gradient: linear-gradient(135deg, #8b5cf6 0%, #3b82f6 100%);\n  --bg: #f1f5f9;\n  --card-bg: #ffffff;\n  --text-main: #0f172a;\n  --text-light: #64748b;\n  --radius-lg: 20px;\n  --radius-md: 12px;\n  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n  --shadow-md: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 4px 6px -2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n  --shadow-hover: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 10px 10px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);\n}\n\nbody {\n  font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--text-main);\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n/* Hero Header */\nheader {\n  background: var(--primary-gradient);\n  color: white;\n  padding: 4rem 1rem 6rem; /* Extra padding at bottom for overlap */\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\nheader h1 {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 3.5rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  letter-spacing: -0.05em;\n}\n\nheader p {\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\n  opacity: 0.9;\n  font-weight: 300;\n  margin-top: 0.5rem;\n}\n\n/* Main Container overlapping the header */\n.container {\n  max-width: 1200px;\n  margin: -4rem auto 3rem; /* Negative top margin pulls cards over the header */\n  padding: 0 1.5rem;\n  position: relative;\n  z-index: 10;\n}\n\n/* Grid Layout */\n#pet-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr));\n  gap: 2.5rem;\n}\n\n/* Card Styling */\n.pet-card {\n  background-color: var(--card-bg);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  overflow: hidden;\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);\n  transition: all 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n\n.pet-card:hover {\n  transform: translateY(-8px);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-hover);\n}\n\n.image-container {\n  position: relative;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 260px;\n}\n\n.pet-image {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  object-fit: cover;\n  background-color: #e2e8f0;\n}\n\n/* Floating Status Badge */\n.pet-status {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 1.25rem;\n  right: 1.25rem;\n  font-size: 0.75rem;\n  padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);\n  backdrop-filter: blur(8px); /* Modern frosted glass effect */\n}\n\n/* Dynamic Badge Colors */\n.status-available { background-color: rgba(220, 252, 231, 0.9); color: #166534; }\n.status-pending { background-color: rgba(254, 240, 138, 0.9); color: #854d0e; }\n.status-adopted { background-color: rgba(241, 245, 249, 0.9); color: #475569; }\n.status-default { background-color: rgba(224, 231, 255, 0.9); color: #4338ca; }\n\n.pet-content {\n  padding: 2rem;\n  flex-grow: 1;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n\n.pet-name {\n  margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;\n  font-size: 2rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--text-main);\n  letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n}\n\n/* Modern Stats Grid */\n.pet-stats {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n  gap: 0.75rem;\n  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n}\n\n.stat-item {\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  padding: 0.75rem;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  color: var(--text-light);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n\n.stat-item strong {\n  color: var(--text-main);\n  font-size: 0.7rem;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;\n}\n\n.pet-bio {\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  color: var(--text-light);\n  line-height: 1.6;\n  margin-top: auto;\n  padding-top: 1.5rem;\n  border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false,
          "type": "support"
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "contents": "document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n  const grid = document.getElementById(\"pet-grid\");\n\n  // Fallback placeholder image URL\n  const placeholderImg = \"https://placehold.co/400x300/e2e8f0/475569?text=No+Image+Available\";\n\n  // Check if 'animals' array exists (in case they broke data.js)\n  if (typeof animals === 'undefined' || !Array.isArray(animals)) {\n    // Inject a styled error message that gets pushed down to the grey background\n    grid.innerHTML = `\n      <div style=\"grid-column: 1/-1; margin-top: 6rem; background-color: #fee2e2; border: 1px solid #fca5a5; color: #b91c1c; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; text-align: center; box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);\">\n        <h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0; font-size: 1.5rem;\">⚠️ Data Error</h3>\n        <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 1.1rem;\">Could not find the <strong>'animals'</strong> array. Please check your <em>data.js</em> file!</p>\n      </div>\n    `;\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Map over the array to create an array of HTML strings\n  const cardsHTML = animals.map(animal => {\n    // Handle Fallbacks for missing data\n    const img = animal.image || placeholderImg;\n    const name = animal.name || \"Unknown Name\";\n    const species = animal.species || \"Unavailable\";\n    const breed = animal.breed || \"Unavailable\";\n    const age = animal.age !== undefined ? animal.age : \"Unavailable\";\n    const gender = animal.gender || \"Unavailable\";\n    const color = animal.color || \"Unavailable\"; \n    const status = animal.status || \"Status Unknown\";\n    const bio = animal.bio || \"No biography available at this time.\";\n\n    // Determine the badge color class based on the status text\n    let badgeClass = \"status-default\";\n    const statusLower = status.toLowerCase();\n    \n    if (statusLower.includes(\"available\")) {\n      badgeClass = \"status-available\";\n    } else if (statusLower.includes(\"pending\")) {\n      badgeClass = \"status-pending\";\n    } else if (statusLower.includes(\"adopted\")) {\n      badgeClass = \"status-adopted\";\n    }\n\n    // Return the HTML string for this specific card using the modern layout\n    return `\n      <div class=\"pet-card\">\n        <div class=\"image-container\">\n          <img src=\"${img}\" alt=\"${name}\" class=\"pet-image\">\n          <span class=\"pet-status ${badgeClass}\">${status}</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"pet-content\">\n          <h2 class=\"pet-name\">${name}</h2>\n          \n          <div class=\"pet-stats\">\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n              <strong>Species</strong>\n              <span>${species}</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n              <strong>Breed</strong>\n              <span>${breed}</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n              <strong>Age</strong>\n              <span>${age}</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n              <strong>Gender</strong>\n              <span>${gender}</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"pet-bio\">\n            ${bio}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    `;\n  }).join(''); // Join the array of HTML strings into one single string\n\n  // Inject the final string into the grid all at once\n  grid.innerHTML = cardsHTML;\n});",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false,
          "type": "support"
        },
        "4": {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "data.js",
          "contents": "const animal = {\n    name: \"Buddy\",\n    species: \"Dog\",\n    breed: \"Golden Retriever\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552053831-71594a27632d?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=400\",\n    age: 3,\n    gender: \"Male\",\n    color: \"Golden\",\n    status: \"Available\",\n    bio: \"Friendly and loves to play fetch. Great with kids and other dogs!\"\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
        "5": {
